+++ b/README.md
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
 Rules: money in integer euro cents; times are ISO-8601 UTC strings; a period covers whole days, so `start` and
 `end` are midnight UTC and `end` (exclusive) is the start of the day after the last day; the same item cannot be
 booked for overlapping periods. Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, …) so behaviour is deterministic.
+A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price (days × `dailyPrice`), rounded to the nearest
+cent with halves rounded up; `quote` and `book` both return the reduced `total`.
 The cancellation policy (no refund under 24 hours before start, otherwise full refund) is not implemented yet.
 
 Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18+, which runs TypeScript directly).
